---
import Dashboard from '../../../layouts/Dashboard.astro';
---

<Dashboard title="API key" active="api-key">
	<div class="alert alert-info mt-6">
		<span>
			Scaffold only. Rotation and revocation are CLI operations until the dashboard has an
			endpoint for them.
		</span>
	</div>

	<div class="card mt-6 bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
		<div class="card-body">
			<h2 class="card-title">Your key</h2>
			<p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
				One key type, sent in the <code class="font-mono">X-API-Key</code> header.
			</p>
			<div class="join mt-2 w-full">
				<input
					type="password"
					value="sk_live_0000000000000000"
					readonly
					aria-label="API key"
					class="input join-item input-bordered w-full font-mono"
				/>
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-primary join-item">Reveal</button>
			</div>
			<div class="card-actions mt-4">
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Rotate</button>
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm text-error">Revoke</button>
			</div>
			<p class="mt-2 text-xs text-base-content/60">
				Revocation is immediate and total, and a revoked key returns the same 401 as an
				unknown one.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="card mt-6 bg-base-100 shadow-sm">
		<div class="card-body">
			<h2 class="card-title">Key properties</h2>
			<ul class="list-inside list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70">
				<li>Per-key rate limit, so one integrator cannot exhaust another's.</li>
				<li>Embedding the key in a client app means it can be extracted — that trade is deliberate.</li>
				<li>Ask for a higher limit and we set it on the key.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</div>
</Dashboard>